<title>USA: U.S. cotton ginnings - USDA.</title>
<headline>U.S. cotton ginnings - USDA.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1996-10-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>USDA reported all U.S. cotton ginnings prior to Oct. 15 with comparison (running bales, linters not included. W-withheld):</p>
<p>			1996	  1995</p>
<p>	  Al     174,950	133,100</p>
<p>	  Az     123,300	101,500</p>
<p>	  Ar     718,600	520,850</p>
<p>	  Ca     231,800	 72,050</p>
<p>	 Fla	14,150	 19,650</p>
<p>	  Ga     346,300	413,100</p>
<p>	  La     642,000	727,800</p>
<p>Cotton Ginnings continued -- (running bales):</p>
<p>			  1996	 1995</p>
<p> Ms		 1,027,450   1,083,150</p>
<p> Mo		   177,400     115,700</p>
<p> NM		    12,950	 3,500</p>
<p> NC		   118,100     114,150</p>
<p> Ok			 W	     150</p>
<p> SC		   132,100	65,250</p>
<p> Tn		   350,050     238,050</p>
<p> Tx		   703,300   1,166,750</p>
<p> US		 4,788,000   4,794,850</p>
<p>Cotton Ginnings continued --</p>
<p>USDA also reported American Pima cotton ginnings:</p>
<p>			  1996	     1995</p>
<p>	 Az	    7,100	    2,900</p>
<p>	 Ca	   10,700		W</p>
<p>	 NM		 W		 W</p>
<p>	 TX		 W	     2,000</p>
<p>	 U.S.	 20,550	    5,250</p>
<p>W - Withheld to avoid disclosing individual gins</p>
</text>
